WEBVTT

00:00:00.593 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.719 --> 00:00:04.785
In this lesson, we do a basic facial, step by step,

00:00:04.735 --> 00:00:08.510
for a client with combination skin that is slightly dehydrated.

00:00:08.766 --> 00:00:12.510
For the timing of each product, always follow the brand's instructions.

00:00:13.089 --> 00:00:13.882
Step one:

00:00:14.054 --> 00:00:14.922
preparation.

00:00:15.417 --> 00:00:17.562
Wipe and disinfect the bed surface.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:22.202
Lay a clean sheet, clean towels, and a clean headband for the new client.

00:00:22.549 --> 00:00:24.202
Set everything out on the trolley:

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:27.931
cotton pads, towels, bowls, brushes, spatulas,

00:00:27.881 --> 00:00:31.642
and the products chosen after the skin analysis.

00:00:32.231 --> 00:00:35.787
Check that the steamer has enough water, the warm towels are ready,

00:00:35.737 --> 00:00:37.722
and the room is warm and comfortable.

00:00:37.979 --> 00:00:39.505
Prepare everything beforehand,

00:00:39.455 --> 00:00:43.242
so you never have to leave the client lying there while you look for things.

00:00:43.825 --> 00:00:44.528
Step two:

00:00:44.836 --> 00:00:45.888
settle the client.

00:00:46.275 --> 00:00:49.987
The client lies on her back, covered with a towel and a blanket,

00:00:49.937 --> 00:00:52.848
leaving only the face, neck and shoulders exposed.

00:00:53.513 --> 00:00:55.568
Put on a headband to hold back the hair.

00:00:56.075 --> 00:00:59.328
Ask whether she is warm enough, and whether the pillow is comfortable.

00:00:59.796 --> 00:01:01.257
If she wears contact lenses,

00:01:01.207 --> 00:01:04.128
ask her to take them out before you work around the eyes.

00:01:04.377 --> 00:01:08.448
Then wash your hands with soap and dry them, as in the hand hygiene lesson.

00:01:09.043 --> 00:01:09.822
Step three:

00:01:10.083 --> 00:01:11.022
makeup removal.

00:01:11.487 --> 00:01:12.622
Start with the eyes.

00:01:12.723 --> 00:01:16.128
Place a cotton pad soaked in makeup remover on the closed eye,

00:01:16.078 --> 00:01:18.942
and hold it for a few seconds to soften the mascara.

00:01:19.361 --> 00:01:22.871
Then wipe gently downward, without rubbing or pulling the skin,

00:01:22.821 --> 00:01:25.342
and without letting product run into the eye.

00:01:25.846 --> 00:01:28.222
Then the lips, wiped very gently.

00:01:28.717 --> 00:01:31.582
After that, remove makeup from the whole face.

00:01:32.176 --> 00:01:33.025
Step four:

00:01:33.196 --> 00:01:34.305
the second cleanse.

00:01:34.754 --> 00:01:40.266
Put cleanser into your palm, warm it, then apply it to the face and neck in small,

00:01:40.216 --> 00:01:41.265
gentle circles,

00:01:41.378 --> 00:01:44.625
working from the chin up to the cheeks, then the forehead.

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:48.625
Light, even pressure, both hands mirroring each other.

00:01:48.888 --> 00:01:49.905
Avoid the eyes.

00:01:50.097 --> 00:01:54.305
Remove it with warm, damp sponges, until no cleanser is left.

00:01:54.966 --> 00:01:55.917
Step five:

00:01:56.184 --> 00:02:00.157
a quick analysis under the magnifying lamp, on freshly cleansed skin.

00:02:00.732 --> 00:02:02.477
Compare with the consultation form:

00:02:02.861 --> 00:02:07.357
has anything changed, are there any red, sore or broken areas today?

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:12.317
For how to analyze each area, see the skin analysis and consultation lesson.

00:02:12.815 --> 00:02:17.277
If you see anything worrying, stop, as in the lesson on when not to treat a client.

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:18.727
Step six:

00:02:18.837 --> 00:02:19.847
exfoliation.

00:02:20.105 --> 00:02:22.407
Choose the type based on the skin analysis:

00:02:22.673 --> 00:02:25.926
today the skin is slightly dehydrated, so choose a gentle one.

00:02:26.265 --> 00:02:28.167
Place cotton pads over the eyes.

00:02:28.345 --> 00:02:32.487
Use a brush to apply a thin layer, avoiding the eye area and the lips.

00:02:32.914 --> 00:02:36.247
Leave it on for the time the brand states, and keep watching the skin.

00:02:36.584 --> 00:02:40.807
If the client feels stinging, or the skin reddens quickly, remove it at once.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:43.127
Then wipe it off with warm sponges.

00:02:43.729 --> 00:02:44.648
Step seven:

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:46.008
warm the skin.

00:02:46.481 --> 00:02:49.208
Test the warmth of the towel on your own wrist first.

00:02:49.557 --> 00:02:53.313
Lay the warm towel over the face, leaving the nose and mouth free,

00:02:53.263 --> 00:02:55.448
so the client can breathe comfortably,

00:02:55.557 --> 00:02:56.968
and hold it there for a moment.

00:02:57.233 --> 00:02:58.248
Or use steam:

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:01.848
place the machine far enough from the face, for a short time.

00:03:02.197 --> 00:03:05.688
For sensitive skin, or skin that is red, skip this step.

00:03:06.355 --> 00:03:07.142
Step eight:

00:03:07.404 --> 00:03:11.142
extractions, only if you have been trained, and the salon allows it.

00:03:11.481 --> 00:03:12.422
Put on gloves.

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:14.742
Wrap soft tissue around your fingertips.

00:03:15.091 --> 00:03:18.102
Press very gently on both sides of the blackhead.

00:03:18.363 --> 00:03:19.622
If it comes out, good;

00:03:19.971 --> 00:03:21.142
if not, leave it.

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:25.142
No nails, no hard squeezing, and keep it very short.

00:03:25.489 --> 00:03:29.782
Afterwards, wipe the area with a soothing product, as the brand instructs.

00:03:29.952 --> 00:03:34.902
If you use an extractor, it must be a sterilized one, taken from a sealed pouch.

00:03:35.385 --> 00:03:39.424
If you have not been trained, skip this step, and note it in the record,

00:03:39.374 --> 00:03:41.142
so someone qualified can do it.

00:03:41.667 --> 00:03:42.517
Step nine:

00:03:42.625 --> 00:03:43.397
the mask.

00:03:43.772 --> 00:03:47.380
Today the skin is combination, with a few blackheads on the nose,

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:49.077
so choose a mask that suits it.

00:03:49.421 --> 00:03:54.451
Apply it evenly with a brush, from the neck up to the chin, the cheeks, the nose,

00:03:54.401 --> 00:03:55.557
then the forehead.

00:03:55.906 --> 00:03:58.597
Leave out the eyes, the nostrils and the lips.

00:03:58.866 --> 00:04:00.357
Leave it on for the brand's time.

00:04:00.589 --> 00:04:04.640
While you wait, you can gently massage the client's hands or shoulders,

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:06.837
but don't leave her alone for too long.

00:04:07.475 --> 00:04:08.280
Step ten:

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:14.840
remove the mask with warm, damp sponges, gently, area by area, without rubbing hard.

00:04:15.429 --> 00:04:19.232
Check around the hairline, under the chin, and beside the nostrils,

00:04:19.182 --> 00:04:21.080
the places that are often missed.

00:04:21.509 --> 00:04:22.680
Then look at the skin again:

00:04:23.176 --> 00:04:28.200
if any area has turned very red, note it, and choose a very gentle moisturizer.

00:04:28.869 --> 00:04:29.734
Step eleven:

00:04:29.959 --> 00:04:32.214
toner, wiped on gently with cotton.

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:33.414
Step twelve:

00:04:33.526 --> 00:04:34.454
moisturizer.

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:39.455
Take the cream out of the jar with a clean spatula, put it on the back of your hand,

00:04:39.405 --> 00:04:41.174
then apply it with light strokes,

00:04:41.283 --> 00:04:42.374
upward and outward.

00:04:42.878 --> 00:04:45.894
If it is daytime, apply sunscreen as the last step.

00:04:46.485 --> 00:04:47.506
Step thirteen:

00:04:47.697 --> 00:04:49.826
aftercare advice, and the next booking.

00:04:50.291 --> 00:04:52.146
Help the client sit up slowly.

00:04:52.318 --> 00:04:52.946
Tell her:

00:04:53.149 --> 00:04:56.826
for the next few days, no exfoliating at home, avoid the sun,

00:04:56.776 --> 00:04:59.026
and remember sunscreen every morning.

00:04:59.528 --> 00:05:04.306
If redness or stinging lasts, or it itches, let the salon know right away.

00:05:04.556 --> 00:05:06.974
And if the skin reacts right there in the salon,

00:05:06.924 --> 00:05:08.946
do what the incidents lesson showed you.

00:05:09.201 --> 00:05:11.506
Then book the next appointment right at the desk.

00:05:12.177 --> 00:05:13.271
Step fourteen:

00:05:13.594 --> 00:05:14.151
clean up.

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:15.751
Put on gloves.

00:05:16.054 --> 00:05:20.150
Towels, headbands and bed linen go into a laundry basket with a lid.

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:24.551
Cotton, tissues and single-use spatulas go into a bin with a lid.

00:05:24.895 --> 00:05:27.511
Brushes and bowls are washed, then disinfected.

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:30.295
Extractors go to be cleaned and sterilized,

00:05:30.245 --> 00:05:32.791
as in the lesson on tools after every client.

00:05:33.045 --> 00:05:37.832
Finally, write in the client record which products were used, how the skin reacted,

00:05:37.782 --> 00:05:39.031
and the advice given.

00:05:39.333 --> 00:05:40.471
Then wash your hands.

00:05:40.728 --> 00:05:43.591
And now, please take the short quiz below the video.
